# Regenerated from the PDF in one command; no reason to version 1.7MB of them:
#   pdftoppm -png -r 100 poster_jiaming_wei.pdf preview_full
#   pdftoppm -png -r 55  poster_jiaming_wei.pdf preview
#   pdftoppm -png -r 14  poster_jiaming_wei.pdf far      # 3m-distance check
preview*.png
far-*.png
mid-*.png
zoom-*.png
# 300dpi raster of the thesis system diagram; poster_figures.py regenerates it
figures/poster_overview.png
# a colleague's example poster, shown for reference — not ours to version
95529.png
# v9 raster assets are VERSIONED, deliberately. The rule this file uses elsewhere
# — "one command regenerates it, so don't store it" — does not hold for these:
# three of their inputs (results/phantom_paper/figures/, results/phantom_paper/
# *.json, results/repro_replicates/) are themselves gitignored experiment data.
# A fresh clone can rebuild the poster from figures/v9/ but cannot rebuild
# figures/v9/ itself. 3.0MB is the price of the poster staying reproducible.
# example posters shown for reference — a colleague's and the supervisor's, not ours to version
117982.png
